# node_modules/, dist/, release/ below have NO leading slash, so each
# matches a directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH, not just at the repo root
# -- this silently swallowed tools/release/ for an entire session (an
# unrelated new tool directory happened to share release/'s bare name) with
# no error, no warning: `git status` simply never mentioned it, so it read
# as "the tool doesn't exist" in every clone despite being present on disk.
# Confirm with `git check-ignore -v <path>` before assuming a new directory
# is tracked. If you need a NEW top-level dir literally named node_modules,
# dist, release, or matching server.log/npm-install.log anywhere below repo
# root, anchor your own pattern with a leading slash (see /private/ below)
# so it does not also swallow something with a plausible-but-different name.
node_modules/
# LIVE generations use a dependency symlink on Linux. A trailing-slash rule
# ignores directories/Windows junctions but not that symlink. Ignore only the
# same top-level dependency mount; source and runtime-byte checks stay intact.
/node_modules
dist/
release/
# A second build output used when release/win-unpacked is held open by another
# process (other Claude sessions' MCP servers read the workspace .mcp.json, which
# the app rewrites to point at whatever build it last ran from). Same artifacts,
# same gitignore reasons.
release-cut/
server.log
npm-install.log
# The Codex CLI cloud client writes error.log here on a failed run. It is a
# diagnostic artifact, never product bytes, and as an untracked file it fails
# tools/require-clean-tree.mjs and so blocks the packaged build outright.
#
# It must also never be committed for a second and harder reason: it records
# account identifiers and the parsed GitHub origin, which carries the owner's
# real name. That is exactly what check-no-owner-data refuses to ship. The
# engine tree already ignores this filename; this worktree carries its own
# .gitignore and did not, so the same file was safe there and a blocker here.
error.log
# The gated-dist run writes .dist-gated.log beside the repo root. Same trap as
# error.log directly above: a diagnostic artifact, never product bytes, and as
# an untracked file it makes `git status --porcelain` non-empty -- which
# require-clean-tree.mjs reads as "any output at all means dirty" and refuses,
# so one build's log blocks the NEXT build in that tree. Found 2026-08-17 with
# the file sitting untracked in this checkout after a dist run.
.dist-gated.log
.dist.log
/private/
# The staged capability payload. Derived output, like dist/ and release/:
# `npm run pack:capability` cuts it fresh from the capability-layer source
# tree, so committing it would freeze a copy that silently stops matching the
# code it was cut from. Anchored with a leading slash, per the warning above,
# because "capability" is a plausible name for a future source directory and a
# bare pattern would swallow it at any depth.
#
# It also must not be committed for a second and harder reason: until the
# capability-layer source is purged, the staged payload carries the builder's
# name, home-directory paths and LAN addresses. The packer marks such a payload
# UNSHIPPABLE-OWNER-DATA.txt and `npm run dist` refuses it, but neither of
# those would stop a `git add -A`. This line does.
/capability/

# Harness output: tools/owner-popup-qa.cjs writes screenshots here by default and
# tools/packaged-qa-suite.mjs can be pointed here with --logs. Untracked files
# fail tools/require-clean-tree.mjs and so block `npm run dist` outright -- the
# same trap error.log above was added for. Anchored with a leading slash, per the
# warning at the top of this file, so it cannot swallow a future tools/artifacts/.
/artifacts/

# QA run outputs, same class as /artifacts/ above: written by the accessibility
# and keyboard harnesses on every run. Evidence, not source; untracked files here
# fail require-clean-tree and block `npm run dist`.
/reports/a11y/
/reports/a11y-keyboard-last-run.json

# offline-routes-qa rewrites its route transcript here on every run;
# a harness-owned artifact must not hold require-clean-tree hostage.
/reports/lanes/team2-b7-transcript.json

# Same class again, 2026-08-19: the 272-tool agent sweep streams its per-batch
# events and summaries here while it runs, and the node-removal drive writes its
# screenshots here. Both are evidence a harness produces, not source anyone
# reproduces from git -- and both blocked a cut by being untracked.
/reports/agent-tools/
/reports/node-remove-drive/

# Agent working logs. Never product content -- reports/ is the tracked
# evidence directory; this is scratch that must not reach a published cut.
logs/

# Generated immediately before a restricted auxiliary presentation child is
# spawned. It contains the checkout's absolute guard path, so it is runtime
# state and must never be committed or mirrored as portable source.
/auxiliary/presentation/agent-settings.json

# Python test imports create bytecode caches in-place. They are generated
# diagnostics, not source, and must not make the release tree dirty.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# Private, generated portable Python/dependency/model payload. Rebuilt and
# hash-verified by pack:voice; never source, a venv link, or an owner cache.
/voice-runtime/bundle/

# Agent working notes written to the repo root. Product evidence lives in
# reports/, which IS tracked; these are scratch and must not reach a cut.
REPORT-*.md

# Worker 87 lane evidence. TAP transcripts and mutation records; scrubbed of
# profile paths, but this directory is never part of a commit.
/.w87-evidence/

# Worker 87 token-lane scratch: redirected state stores for the end-to-end driver.
/.w87-scratch/
/.w87-scratch-gated/
/.w87-e2e-state/

# Machine-local pointer to this operator's research data server; never a product asset.
public/research-workspace.json
